sub:quote a prov:Entity;
    prov:hadPrimarySource <https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fractastical/delphisci/2404c437f822e1c98420130cd01e7972acf3ac57/books/levin-papers/inputs/2024-collective.txt#line=48,49>;
    prov:wasQuotedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-024-06037-4>;
    <https://schema.org/text> "In all of the many studies on perturbation of the LR pathway, we are aware of only one that actually breaks the concordance: disruption of the planar polarity pathway by down-regulating VANGL signaling149 leads to a speckling on both sides of the midline, consistent with individual cells within a single lateral domain disagreeing on whether they should have L or R identity (Fig. 6a–d).".
